# Line-ending policy.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, which converts LF -> CRLF on checkout.
# For shell scripts that silently breaks execution: `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a valid
# interpreter, so a fresh clone would get a pre-commit hook that never runs —
# taking the index.html data-loss guard and the repo-integrity check with it.
# Pin the formats that care, and leave everything else to autocrlf.

# Shell scripts and git hooks must stay LF or they will not execute.
*.sh            text eol=lf
.githooks/**    text eol=lf

# Windows batch genuinely requires CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.webm          binary
*.mp4           binary
*.pem           binary
